### 6.2 State Badge Rendering
After implementing the content component, you MUST implement Badge rendering for state fields in detail components.

**State Badge Implementation**:
When state fields are present in the detail component, you MUST update the content.js file to render state values as Badges:

```javascript
// In src/[module]/detail/content.js
import { Badge } from "uu5g05-elements";

// Add toCamelCase method to Content component
toCamelCase(str) {
  if (!str) return str;
  return str
    .toLowerCase()
    .replace(/[-_\s]+(.)?/g, (_, char) => (char ? char.toUpperCase() : ''))
    .replace(/^(.)/, (char) => char.toUpperCase());
},

// Add getStateColorScheme method to Content component
getStateColorScheme(state) {
  switch (state?.toLowerCase()) {
    case "active":
    case "running":
      return "green";
    case "inactive":
    case "stopped":
      return "red";
    case "pending":
    case "waiting":
      return "orange";
    case "completed":
    case "finished":
      return "blue";
    default:
      return "cyan";
  }
},

// Update InfoGroup itemList to render state as Badge
const itemList = [
  { subtitle: lsi.oid, ...addHrefIfUri(data.oid) },
  { subtitle: lsi.name, ...addHrefIfUri(data.name) },
  // ... other basic fields
  {
    subtitle: lsi.state,
    title: data.state ? (
      <Badge colorScheme={Content.getStateColorScheme(data.state)} size="xl">
        {Content.toCamelCase(data.state)}
      </Badge>
    ) : null
  },
  // ... more basic fields
];
```

**Purpose**: This ensures that state fields in detail components are rendered as prominent, color-coded badges with proper CamelCase formatting for better user experience and visual clarity.

### 6.3 DateTime Rendering
After implementing the content component, you MUST render date and datetime fields using the DateTime component in detail components.

**DateTime Rendering Implementation**:
When date or datetime fields are present in the detail component, you MUST update the content.js file to use DateTime component:

```javascript
// In src/[module]/detail/content.js
import { InfoGroup, ListLayout, DateTime } from "uu5g05-elements";

// Update InfoGroup itemList to render date fields with DateTime component
const itemList = [
  // ... other fields
  { 
    subtitle: lsi.dateField, 
    title: data.dateField ? <DateTime value={data.dateField} dateFormat="short" timeFormat="none" /> : null 
  },
  { 
    subtitle: lsi.datetimeField, 
    title: data.datetimeField ? <DateTime value={data.datetimeField} dateFormat="short" timeFormat="none" /> : null 
  },
  // ... more fields
];
```

**Purpose**: This ensures that date and datetime fields in detail components are rendered using the proper DateTime component for consistent formatting and better user experience.

