## 7. Best Practices

- **Always confirm specifications** before starting implementation
- **Use cmd /c wrapper** for uu5Generate commands
- **Implement hybrid content approach** using InfoGroup for basic fields and Grid for nested objects
- **Make URIs clickable** by detecting and adding href properties
- **Exclude system attributes** (sysCts, sysMts, sysRev) from display
- **Use Badge components** for state fields with proper color schemes
- **Use DateTime components** for all date/datetime fields
- **Test with real data** before considering implementation complete
- **Format and compile** after each major change

## 8. Troubleshooting

| Issue | Cause | Solution |
|-------|-------|----------|
| uu5Generate prompts for input | Missing parameters | Always include ALL parameters (--sub-app, --brick-uu5-tag, --redirect-uu5-route) |
| PowerShell command fails | Using PowerShell directly | Always use cmd /c wrapper for uu5Generate commands |
| Data not displaying | Wrong data access pattern | Check both [module]Dto.data and [module]Dto for data |
| WorkspaceProvider errors | Unnecessary workspace dependency | Remove WorkspaceProvider and use baseUri directly |
| URIs not clickable | Missing href detection | Implement addHrefIfUri helper function |
| State values not showing as badges | Missing Badge import or helpers | Import Badge and add helper methods (toCamelCase, getStateColorScheme) |
| Dates not formatting correctly | Not using DateTime component | Import and use DateTime component for all date fields |
| Compilation fails | Syntax errors or missing imports | Fix imports, check syntax, and re-run build |
| Demo page not working | Missing configuration or test data | Configure BASE_URI and identifier value for demo |